
========================================================================
  COMPLEMENT ASYMMETRY AT n=5
========================================================================

  For each labeled tiling T:
  - w(T) = which arcs are neutral (wiggly self-loop)
  - w(T^op) = which arcs are neutral in the complement
  - asymmetry = Hamming distance between w(T) and w(complement(T))

  COMPLEMENT ASYMMETRY PER MERGED CLASS:

  mid | H   | SC? | avg_hamm | avg_n_T  | avg_n_Top | Jaccard  | same_n? 
  ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  0   | 1   | SC  | 0.00     | 4.00     | 4.00     | 1.0000   | YES
  1   | 3   | NS  | 0.00     | 1.00     | 1.00     | 1.0000   | YES
  2   | 5   | NS  | 0.00     | 3.00     | 3.00     | 1.0000   | YES
  3   | 3   | SC  | 0.00     | 0.00     | 0.00     | 1.0000   | YES
  4   | 9   | SC  | 0.00     | 2.00     | 2.00     | 1.0000   | YES
  5   | 9   | SC  | 0.00     | 0.00     | 0.00     | 1.0000   | YES
  6   | 11  | SC  | 0.00     | 2.00     | 2.00     | 1.0000   | YES
  7   | 15  | SC  | 0.00     | 0.00     | 0.00     | 1.0000   | YES
  8   | 13  | SC  | 0.00     | 0.00     | 0.00     | 1.0000   | YES
  9   | 15  | SC  | 0.00     | 0.00     | 0.00     | 1.0000   | YES

